  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Compounds given in option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;chain isomers.</p><p>Compounds given in option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;are not isomers since molecular formula is not same.</p><p>Compounds given in option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;are position isomers.</p><p>Distribution of alkyl groups around polyvalent functional group&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>CO</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COO</mi><mo>-</mo><mtext>&#160;etc.</mtext><mo>)</mo></math>give rise to metamers and phenomenon is called metamerism.<img src=\"assets\\st0241_461ef1b1a70d.png\" style=\"width: 403px; height: 152px;\" /></p>"
